WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:02.120
He was the one who started it all.

00:00:02.220 --> 00:00:03.420
Will he be the one to end it?

00:00:03.510 --> 00:00:07.980
While many fans are speculating that a heavyweight
hero like Hulk or Captain Marvel will be the

00:00:07.990 --> 00:00:12.190
one to ultimately bring down the Mad Titan,
there are numerous reasons why Thanos should

00:00:12.190 --> 00:00:13.500
fear Iron Man the most.

00:00:14.660 --> 00:00:19.211
Stark first caught Thanos' attention after
thwarting his original invasion of Earth back

00:00:19.220 --> 00:00:20.500
in the first Avengers film.

00:00:20.580 --> 00:00:24.840
Even though Thanos himself wasn't present
at the invasion, Stark's heroic actions still

00:00:24.840 --> 00:00:29.410
ultimately foiled the Mad Titan's plans of
conquering Earth and claiming the Tesseract

00:00:29.410 --> 00:00:30.120
for himself.

00:00:30.410 --> 00:00:34.480
A being as driven and powerful as Thanos would
surely make a point to remember anyone tenacious

00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:35.900
enough to defy his whims.

00:00:36.060 --> 00:00:40.789
This is exactly why Thanos knew who Tony Stark
was during Avengers: Infinity War, as confirmed

00:00:40.789 --> 00:00:44.240
by Joe Russo during the commentary track for
the film's home release.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:45.720
"Stark."

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:46.880
"You know me?"

00:00:47.660 --> 00:00:48.500
"I do."

00:00:48.989 --> 00:00:52.940
Russo went on to describe the "existential
connection" between the two that has stemmed

00:00:52.940 --> 00:00:54.379
from that first conflict.

00:00:54.379 --> 00:00:58.539
The fact that Stark is the only Avenger that
Thanos knows and addresses by name already

00:00:58.540 --> 00:01:01.600
shows that the Mad Titan views him as a potential
threat.

00:01:02.620 --> 00:01:06.660
Back in Age of Ultron, Tony Stark actually
predicted the events of Infinity War with

00:01:06.660 --> 00:01:08.020
frightening accuracy.

00:01:08.080 --> 00:01:12.380
During a heated exchange with Steve Rogers,
Tony's concerns about an unstoppable threat

00:01:12.390 --> 00:01:16.729
from space not only referenced the Battle
of New York, but also foreshadowed the arrival

00:01:16.729 --> 00:01:17.760
of the Mad Titan.

00:01:18.140 --> 00:01:19.140
"We're the Avengers.

00:01:19.740 --> 00:01:24.600
We can bust arms dealers all the live-long
day, but that up there?

00:01:24.620 --> 00:01:26.060
That's the endgame."

00:01:26.700 --> 00:01:31.520
Not only did Stark predict the title of Endgame
during this verbal tirade, he also foretold

00:01:31.540 --> 00:01:33.340
their defeat at the hands of Thanos.

00:01:34.960 --> 00:01:35.480
"We'll lose."

00:01:37.020 --> 00:01:38.820
"Then we'll do that together, too."

00:01:39.680 --> 00:01:43.640
The Avengers eventually give it all they have,
but they weren't enough to stop the Mad Titan

00:01:43.640 --> 00:01:45.469
from collecting the Infinity Stones.

00:01:45.469 --> 00:01:49.369
Rogers might be the courageous leader who
the heroes look up to in the darkest of times,

00:01:49.369 --> 00:01:53.780
but Stark is the only realist on the team
trying to plan ahead before disaster strikes.

00:01:53.780 --> 00:01:58.479
Tony's uncanny ability to realistically anticipate
what the future holds is another reason Thanos

00:01:58.480 --> 00:01:59.520
should be wary of him.

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:05.680
Long ago, Thanos foresaw the downfall of his
own civilization due to overpopulation and

00:02:05.680 --> 00:02:07.329
exhaustion of resources.

00:02:07.329 --> 00:02:12.510
Despite his best efforts, the people of Titan
wouldn't listen to his call for action, understandably,

00:02:12.510 --> 00:02:15.450
due to his radical idea of eliminating half
the population.

00:02:15.450 --> 00:02:19.700
Although Stark's ideas were drastically different
from Thanos', it was the same fear for his

00:02:19.700 --> 00:02:22.440
people that drove him to misguidedly create
Ultron.

00:02:22.440 --> 00:02:27.140
Tony created the murder bot to combat future
threats, but in doing so, he was giving into

00:02:27.150 --> 00:02:31.730
the very same kind of fear that drove Thanos
to concoct his genocide of "balance."

00:02:31.730 --> 00:02:36.069
This is yet another reason that Thanos fears
Stark, he respects Tony's efforts to protect

00:02:36.069 --> 00:02:40.280
his planet, and knows that the Iron Avenger
will stop at nothing to defend Earth.

00:02:41.180 --> 00:02:43.700
"The hardest choices require the strongest
will."

00:02:45.600 --> 00:02:49.840
Throughout the grand arc of the MCU, Stark
has steadily improved his suits to adapt to

00:02:49.840 --> 00:02:51.800
various threats and situations.

00:02:51.900 --> 00:02:56.320
Tony's knack for modifying his tech was highlighted
in the first Iron Man film when he faced off

00:02:56.320 --> 00:02:58.980
against Obadiah Stane's Iron Monger armor.

00:02:59.100 --> 00:03:03.920
After realizing that his titanium-steel Mark
2 armor would freeze up at high altitudes,

00:03:03.920 --> 00:03:08.400
Stark reconfigures it using a gold-titanium
alloy that could endure lower temperatures.

00:03:08.569 --> 00:03:12.480
This small tweak helps Tony defeat Stane by
luring him up high into the atmosphere, where

00:03:12.480 --> 00:03:14.640
his nemesis' suit freezes over.

00:03:15.060 --> 00:03:16.420
"How'd you solve the icing problem?"

00:03:16.980 --> 00:03:18.280
"Icing problem?"

00:03:20.860 --> 00:03:21.900
"Might want to look into it."

00:03:24.040 --> 00:03:29.140
Stark uses this innate adaptability to turn
his perceived failures into learning experiences.

00:03:29.150 --> 00:03:33.220
During Avengers: Civil War, James Rhodes suffers
critical injuries after being shot down in

00:03:33.220 --> 00:03:34.519
his War Machine armor.

00:03:34.519 --> 00:03:38.650
So Tony develops a parachute for the Iron
Spider armor he gives to Peter Parker in Infinity

00:03:38.650 --> 00:03:39.140
War.

00:03:39.200 --> 00:03:44.600
After Ant-Man shrinks down and damages his
suit during Civil War, Tony switches to nanotechnology.

00:03:44.600 --> 00:03:49.020
After being defeated in hand-to-hand combat
by Steve Rogers and Bucky Barnes, he learns

00:03:49.030 --> 00:03:53.849
to use his nanotech to create melee weapons
around his hands, such as battering rams,

00:03:53.849 --> 00:03:55.080
blades, and shields.

00:03:55.080 --> 00:03:58.260
Each defeat and failure that Stark endures
only makes him stronger.

00:03:59.480 --> 00:04:03.920
One fan theory claims there is evidence Tony
uses the Infinity Stones in the future.

00:04:03.920 --> 00:04:04.920
The evidence?

00:04:04.920 --> 00:04:07.470
The fact that his left arm has bothered him
in previous films.

00:04:07.470 --> 00:04:11.510
As we see at the end of Infinity War, even
Thanos himself is wounded by the exertion

00:04:11.510 --> 00:04:12.940
of carrying out the Decimation.

00:04:13.209 --> 00:04:17.240
If Tony attempted to reverse the snap using
the Infinity Stones, chances are it would

00:04:17.240 --> 00:04:19.860
seriously injure, if not completely obliterate
him.

00:04:20.040 --> 00:04:24.160
The force of using the Infinity Stones could
be so powerful that the pain reverberates

00:04:24.160 --> 00:04:27.580
through time, and Tony feels some type of
ominous ripple effect.

00:04:28.240 --> 00:04:29.120
"My left arm is numb.

00:04:29.120 --> 00:04:29.760
Is that normal?"

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:34.800
Iron Man wielding the Infinity Gauntlet would
come full circle with the comics, in which

00:04:34.800 --> 00:04:38.480
he has used it before to defeat a bad guy
who calls himself the Hood.

00:04:39.460 --> 00:04:43.420
From the Endgame trailers, we know Tony is
drifting through space in the Benatar with

00:04:43.420 --> 00:04:43.920
Nebula.

00:04:43.920 --> 00:04:48.040
As the adopted daughter of Thanos, she has
incredibly intimate knowledge about the abusive

00:04:48.040 --> 00:04:48.800
Mad Titan.

00:04:48.960 --> 00:04:52.560
Even though she might not be aware of it,
Nebula could hold the secret to defeating

00:04:52.560 --> 00:04:56.240
Thanos, a secret that only someone as brilliant
as Stark could deduce.

00:04:56.240 --> 00:05:00.560
Pairing together Nebula with Iron Man is no
coincidence, especially since the Russo brothers

00:05:00.560 --> 00:05:03.180
confirmed that she plays an important role
in the plot.

00:05:03.400 --> 00:05:04.500
They told The Telegraph:

00:05:04.580 --> 00:05:08.140
"When you're dealing with characters like
Nebula, a child of Thanos, it's impossible

00:05:08.150 --> 00:05:11.710
not to make her integral to the story or have
an emotional connection to it."

00:05:11.710 --> 00:05:16.080
Although Thanos probably does not have any
type of obvious weakness, Stark could utilize

00:05:16.080 --> 00:05:20.370
Nebula's knowledge of her adopted father to
get inside his head and predict his next move.

00:05:21.630 --> 00:05:26.660
When the first Iron Man movie back in 2008
led the charge of the Marvel Cinematic Universe,

00:05:26.660 --> 00:05:30.569
Tony Stark's actions essentially kicked off
the series of events that led to Infinity

00:05:30.569 --> 00:05:31.060
War.

00:05:31.160 --> 00:05:35.400
Even though Tony could have never predicted
how far his superhero adventures would take

00:05:35.400 --> 00:05:38.840
him, it would certainly be poetic for the
one who started it all to end it.

00:05:39.200 --> 00:05:39.700
"My turn."

00:05:44.880 --> 00:05:48.760
Tony Stark was a completely different person
when he first hit the scene, and his character

00:05:48.760 --> 00:05:50.230
arc is one of redemption.

00:05:50.230 --> 00:05:54.150
From his history as a weapons developer to
his guilt over the lives lost due to the Avengers'

00:05:54.150 --> 00:05:58.680
actions in Sokovia, Stark has felt an increasing
amount of responsibility for the suffering

00:05:58.680 --> 00:05:59.240
around him.

00:05:59.400 --> 00:06:03.080
Although he has made efforts to atone for
his sins, he remains a tortured soul.

00:06:06.020 --> 00:06:07.480
"How did you get out of the wormhole?"

00:06:09.140 --> 00:06:13.100
This need for atonement that has driven Stark
over the past few films could very well be

00:06:13.100 --> 00:06:17.060
building toward the ultimate sacrifice that
he almost made in the first Avengers movie.

00:06:17.160 --> 00:06:21.640
Since Robert Downey Jr.'s contract expires
after Endgame, many fans are speculating that

00:06:21.640 --> 00:06:24.320
Iron Man will sacrifice himself to save the
others.

00:06:25.480 --> 00:06:30.260
When Thanos easily dismantles the entire cast
of Marvel heroes during Infinity War, he seems

00:06:30.260 --> 00:06:33.680
content to simply incapacitate his enemies
instead of murdering them.

00:06:33.780 --> 00:06:38.139
Outside of the snap, the only characters he
ends up killing personally are Heimdall, Loki,

00:06:38.139 --> 00:06:41.639
Gamora, and Vision, each of whom he offs for
a specific reason.

00:06:41.639 --> 00:06:46.370
As the Russo brothers pointed out on the Infinity
War commentary track, Tony is the only Avenger

00:06:46.370 --> 00:06:49.120
that Thanos goes out of his way to try and
kill from the start.

00:06:49.330 --> 00:06:53.580
This is interesting because Iron Man is not
as strong as Hulk or Thor, yet Thanos leaves

00:06:53.600 --> 00:06:55.000
them alive after defeating them.

00:06:55.240 --> 00:06:59.280
Thanos specifically sets out to kill Stark
because he perceives him as a real threat,

00:06:59.280 --> 00:07:00.180
and when he says,

00:07:01.540 --> 00:07:03.020
"I hope they remember you."

00:07:04.280 --> 00:07:05.740
... he seems to think he's succeeded.

00:07:07.040 --> 00:07:11.040
When it comes down to it, the main reason
Thanos respects and fears Tony is simply how

00:07:11.040 --> 00:07:11.900
alike they are.

00:07:12.060 --> 00:07:15.530
The Russo brothers touched upon this during
their interview with The Telegraph.

00:07:15.530 --> 00:07:16.530
Joe Russo said:

00:07:16.530 --> 00:07:20.420
"Tony is the most desperately driven, down
to the core, to react against something like

00:07:20.420 --> 00:07:20.920
Thanos.

00:07:20.920 --> 00:07:25.380
I think this is intrinsic to Tony's psychology,
and because Tony started it all with Iron

00:07:25.380 --> 00:07:28.470
Man, he has a special connection to the threat
that's facing him."

00:07:28.470 --> 00:07:31.830
This is how Thanos knows Tony will do whatever
it takes to stop him.

00:07:31.830 --> 00:07:35.500
The Mad Titan sees too much of himself in
Stark… and that frightens him.

